---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Why Hoagiestack?"
  description="Your newsletter is a small media business. Joe Taylor Jr. of Johns & Taylor on why the parts that matter most should sit on your terms."
>
  <section class="section--cream hero hero--interior" aria-labelledby="page-title">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why Hoagiestack?</p>
      <h1 id="page-title">Your newsletter is a small media business.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Once readers start paying you, you're running one, whether it feels that way or not.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-label="The story">
    <div class="container narrow prose">
      <p>And the parts that matter most (your subscriber list, your archive, how readers pay you, and whether you can leave) can sit on your terms or on somebody else's.</p>
      <p>I called this project Hoagiestack because I think a newsletter should be built around your work and your readers, from ingredients you pick. A premade sub is convenient. You just don't get much say in the recipe.</p>
      <p>I'm Joe Taylor Jr., managing director of <a href="https://johnsandtaylor.com">Johns &amp; Taylor</a>, a user experience and web development agency just outside Philadelphia. I've been building content tools for newsrooms and media businesses since 1998.</p>
      <p>I'm not trying to talk anyone off Substack who's happy there. If you're happy on it and none of these arguments sway you, I won't push you off a platform you like. I'd just like the choice to be a deliberate one.</p>

      <h2>What I look at</h2>
      <p>When I compare publishing setups for clients, a few questions carry most of the weight.</p>
      <ul class="checks">
        <li>Does the tool get out of your way enough that you'll actually publish?</li>
        <li>Can you take your list and your archive with you if you need to leave?</li>
        <li>Do its compromises line up with what you care about, including how much maintenance you're willing to take on?</li>
      </ul>
      <p>There's rarely one right answer, which is why we usually start with a conversation.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand placement="about" heading="Got a half-formed plan? Bring it.">
    <p>Half an hour with our team to talk through your list, your archive, and where you'd like your newsletter to live.</p>
  </CtaBand>
</Base>
